-## 12. Validation
+One summary bullet per feature (or a few for a large one), with links to the reference page. Do not restate rules, limits, or warnings, and do not add a "Behavior changes" bullet that repeats the reference page.
+
+## 12. Single source of truth (new features and impacts)
+
+A new feature is documented in **one place only**: the reference page of the subject (a dedicated concept page for a server/protocol/syntax topic, the command page or class API page for a command/class/function). Decide this page **before writing**; create it if none fits.
+
+Every other page impacted by the feature (concepts, ORDA, Project, compiler, code editor, components, permissions, release notes…):
+- gets **a short sentence or bullet of context + a link** to the reference page anchor (`[text](path.md#anchor)`), saying *that* the feature touches this page and *why*, not *how it behaves*;
+- must NOT contain: rules, option/property lists, type-conversion or other tables, JSON schemas/files, examples, limits, error cases, warnings lists, or step-by-step behavior;
+- must NOT receive a new section longer than ~3 lines. If you are about to write more, move it to the reference page and link instead. Own-page facts stay allowed (e.g. "the compiler also generates file X", "this folder may contain file Y"), followed by a link for the format/rules.
+
+Also:
+- Write each example once, in the reference page.
+- Link to the reference anchor, never to an impacted page or to a copy. Do not move a section to another page without fixing all links (`npm run build -- --locale en` reports broken anchors).
+- If existing content already duplicates the feature, replace it with a link instead of adding a second copy.
+
+## 13. Validation
 
 - `npm run build -- --locale en` (Docusaurus, checks broken links/MDX).
 - CI also runs `syntax-checker` on `docs/` (syntax strings) and `diff_images`.
